
There are 3 examples: one for C/C++ compilers and two for executing in ROOT session.

Example for C/C++ compiler:
Example #1:
	sand_ex1.cpp
	The example uses two external text files and creates a text file with the output spectrum.
	Required external libraries:
		CommonUtils
			function NS_AbsBufCount()
			function NS_AbsBufPtr()
			function NS_AbstractTabCount()
			function NS_AbstractTabPtrX()
			function NS_ReadAbstractFile()
			function NS_WriteAbstractFile()
		FuncUtils
			function NS_PolF()
		SpectrumUtils
			function NS_ReadCalibrationCoeffiecients()
			function NS_SpectrumFini()
			function NS_SpectrumInit()
			function NS_SpectrumSAND()

Examples for ROOT session:
Example #2:
	sand_root_ex1.cpp
	The example uses an external root file with the input spectrum, a text file with calibration coefficients
	and, creates a root file with the output spectrum.
	Required external libraries:
		SpectrumUtils
			function NS_ReadCalibrationCoeffiecients()
			function NS_SpectrumRootFini()
			function NS_SpectrumRootInit()
			function NS_SpectrumSANDRoot()

Example #3:
	sand_root_ex2.cpp
	The example uses an external text file with the input spectrum, creates a root file with the input spectrum and
	a text file with the output spectrum.
	Required external libraries:
		CommonUtils
			function NS_AbsBufCount()
			function NS_AbsBufPtr()
			function NS_AbsBufPushBack()
			function NS_AbstractTabCount()
			function NS_AbstractTabPushBack()
			function NS_ReadAbstractFile()
			function NS_WriteAbstractFile()
		FuncUtils
			function NS_PolF()
		SpectrumUtils
			function NS_SpectrumFini()
			function NS_SpectrumInit()
			function NS_SpectrumRootInit()
			function NS_SpectrumSANDRoot()
